WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:01.880
Hey guys,&nbsp;

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:07.760
What is more important to you - this&nbsp;
temporary world that is passing away?&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.760
Or God?
I want you to answer this question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:20.800
honestly while I explain the following five&nbsp;
things that all Christian men should stop doing.&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.880
Let's start with number one.
Stop pursuing the wrong things.&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:32.880
You could pursue a lot of things in life&nbsp;
... money, relationships, power... but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.920
only one pursuit brings satisfaction on earth&nbsp;
because only one pursuit matters for eternity:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.800
becoming a true man of God.
I wrote that on the back cover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:56.880
of my new book called Bold Pursuit, a 90-day&nbsp;
devotional for men seeking the heart of God.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:06.280
I believe one of the worst things a man can do is&nbsp;
to waste his God-given life to pursue in his head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:11.120
the big things, the small things, according&nbsp;
to his three-pound brain because he thinks he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:18.640
knows better than God to pursue that and to miss&nbsp;
out on what God has actually planned for him.&nbsp;

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.080
And if you think that you know better&nbsp;
than God with your small brain then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:30.440
it's extremely sad because you're missing&nbsp;
out on real purpose and fulfillment and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:35.800
peace and God's blessing because if&nbsp;
you walk in your own way and not in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:42.040
God's way - within His will - then God's&nbsp;
blessing is not going to be on your life.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.920
[Proverbs 3:5-6]

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.600
This is why so many men are complaining.
And they say things like, I don't understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.360
why God is not helping me in this and&nbsp;
maybe it's because you are trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:13.920
force doors open that were never meant&nbsp;
to be opened because that's your will.&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.480
You're not following God's will.
You're not going through the door that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.400
He has actually planned for you and keeping&nbsp;
open for you that you need to go through.&nbsp;

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:26.320
You see, as a reborn Christian,&nbsp;
you need to abide in Christ.&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.240
And then you will produce the right fruit.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:29.760
[John 15:4]

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.800
You see, that is what it means to be a&nbsp;
true child of God and if you are a true&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:54.320
son of God then you don't just think that&nbsp;
God is some part of your life now and then.&nbsp;

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.360
When you feel like it.
He is your life now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.480
because He made you a new creation.
He is the one that directs your paths and you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.920
follow Him with your whole heart and soul.
Do you do that?

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.080
[Galatians 2:20]

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:37.720
Are you a true son of the almighty living God?
You know, sometimes we forget who God is.&nbsp;

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.000
We don't have enough respect for Him.
We just take Him for granted.&nbsp;

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.800
Oh my relationship with God and you&nbsp;
kind of bring Him down to your level.&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.280
He is God.
Do you understand that?&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:53.080
In the Old Testament, only the high priest was&nbsp;
allowed to enter the holy of holies only once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:59.960
a year but now after Jesus came and died on a&nbsp;
cross, and rose from the grave ... now when when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:07.240
we accept Him because of grace, God saves us.
He declares us as righteous and that is why we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:12.760
can all enter the holy of holies because that&nbsp;
is now, you know, there's no temple anymore.&nbsp;

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:20.840
Because our bodies are the temple of God.
And we can approach His throne with confidence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:25.680
but with a lot of respect because&nbsp;
He is still God and He is holy.&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.640
When you live that way, when you put God first in&nbsp;
everything... everything that you do ... suddenly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.640
everything else falls into place.
Everything you do is blessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:42.080
because you put God first and that is&nbsp;
the requirement for all His promises.&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.600
And then when you start to do that -&nbsp;
when you live this life of complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.520
surrender - then you start to realize,&nbsp;
man, now you have everything you need.&nbsp;

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.840
You have fulfillment, you have purpose,&nbsp;
and you have peace that surpasses all&nbsp;

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.800
understanding.
Jesus said:

00:04:58.800 --> 00:04:59.560
[Matthew 16:24]

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:20.280
That is the life of complete surrender and&nbsp;
the only life where you will find true peace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:23.920
that surpasses all understanding even when&nbsp;
you're going through trials and tribulations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:27.880
because you understand.
Because you abide in God.&nbsp;

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:31.440
Him in you, you in Him.
You can see the bigger picture of life.&nbsp;

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.560
Everything starts to make sense.
And you move forward and you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:40.200
see how God is just blessing you and you get the&nbsp;
power to overcome any kind of obstacle that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:46.200
life throws at you because now you're not tackling&nbsp;
these things alone anymore with only your limited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:52.920
power mind capability ... three pound small brain.
A lot of people think they know better than God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:57.520
but now you have the Holy Spirit in you.
The power of God.&nbsp;

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:01.800
He is leading you and helping you.
He is in your corner fighting for you.&nbsp;

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:08.560
Let's move on to the next one.
Stop thinking you are always right.&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:17.120
That kind of arrogant prideful hard attitude&nbsp;
does not fit in with the new Christian lifestyle.&nbsp;

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.520
That might have been part of your old lifestyle -&nbsp;
the person you used to be - but remember you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:29.120
a new creation in Christ and now you are humble.
You live according to the Spirit, not according&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:35.320
to that old sinful flesh that's full&nbsp;
of the ego and the "I" "me-me-me".&nbsp;

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:39.680
Sinful flesh.
There's a change because you love God.&nbsp;

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:43.160
You also love other people because&nbsp;
that's the Holy Spirit in you.&nbsp;

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.880
You know you've received that&nbsp;
unconditional sacrificial love from God.&nbsp;

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.680
Agape love.
And God's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:54.000
love for other people flows through you.
So then you start to understand... man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.840
you need to be the light of the world.
You need to be a sweet smelling aroma so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:03.560
it's more important to win the person than it is&nbsp;
to win the argument in the flesh, full of pride,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:09.240
because you just want to win the argument.
You keep on fighting and you want to be right.&nbsp;

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:14.640
Forgetting that you need to win&nbsp;
the soul of that person for Christ.&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.360
So you might win the argument&nbsp;
but you will lose the person.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:21.440
[Proverbs 16:18]

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:37.040
One of the ugliest things that you can&nbsp;
see is a self-professed Christian man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:42.960
arguing - quarreling with an unbeliever&nbsp;
for example - about religious things.&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.280
But he's doing it through&nbsp;
the flesh, full of pride.&nbsp;

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.480
Full of ego.
Because he wants to win&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:56.040
that conversation, that argument.
And he's not sharing the Gospel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.040 --> 00:08:02.200
taking the lead of the Holy Spirit&nbsp;
in truth and in love, being humble.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.000
[Proverbs 11:2]

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:12.960
[Proverbs 16:5]

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:35.080
You know, there's a lot of people who just want&nbsp;
to keep on fighting, you know. They're like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:39.120
I'm right, I'm right, I'm right.
And they will keep on fighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:44.360
because it is so important for them to be right.
You know that is from the sinful flesh and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.520
when they are right and the other&nbsp;
person says, okay, you're right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:50.360
they will... they will keep on going.
They will say things like, yeah, you see?&nbsp;

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.720
You see?
You see?&nbsp;

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.480
I told you.
Even when things happen at the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:59.240
they're like, I told you this happened.
You don't need to do that.&nbsp;

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:05.440
That kind of attitude is not&nbsp;
part of the new life in Christ.&nbsp;

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.600
Examine yourself - ask yourself&nbsp;
- and be brutally honest.&nbsp;

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:14.920
Do you think you're always right?
Will you argue with them until they see things the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:22.000
way you do because you think you're always right?
If you are, then you need to stop living in sin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.320
because that is sin.
You are quenching the Holy Spirit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:31.800
and you need to obey God, not just in the way in&nbsp;
what you say but also in the way you say things.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.720
[Romans 12:16]

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:51.080
Did you read that?
It says sometimes be wise in your own sight.&nbsp;

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:54.960
No, it didn't say that.
Did it say 50 percent of the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.200
be wise in your own sight?
No.&nbsp;

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:04.040
Did it say one percent of the&nbsp;
time be wise in your own sight?&nbsp;

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:04.920
No.&nbsp;

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:12.560
It says never never never&nbsp;
be wise in your own sight.&nbsp;

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:20.320
No one likes people who think that they are always&nbsp;
right because they reek of puffed up egos and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:25.440
pushes people away from the Gospel.
God actually says in Philippians 2:3:

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.640
[Philippians 2:3-4]

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:55.360
If you truly love God, with everything that&nbsp;
is in you, you will also love other people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.720
and you will care about them.
You will try to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:02.000
things from their perspectives.
You know, the biggest challenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:09.640
for every reborn believer Christian is not&nbsp;
other people or the things in this world.&nbsp;

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:14.160
It is the self-life.
That is why Jesus said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:19.800
if you want to follow Him, you need to deny&nbsp;
yourself, pick up your cross, and follow Him.&nbsp;

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:25.520
Pick up your cross - that means you&nbsp;
need to crucify yourself with Jesus.&nbsp;

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.960
That old sinful flesh.
Let's move on to the next one.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:40.120
Stop making excuses for your fleshly nature.
Christian men do that a lot more than they think.&nbsp;

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:44.680
For example, some make excuses or&nbsp;
lie like the rest of the world.&nbsp;

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:48.400
They get to work late and then they&nbsp;
say things like, sorry, I'm late.&nbsp;

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.920
It was traffic.
Well, they actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:56.120
have a cup of coffee takeaway in their hand,&nbsp;
meaning they took 10 to 20 minutes to buy that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.120 --> 00:12:02.440
coffee and also knowing that everyone else&nbsp;
in a meeting had to sit in the same traffic.&nbsp;

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:06.840
So it's just an excuse.
That's not the reason why you're late.&nbsp;

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:10.360
The reason you're late is because you&nbsp;
took some time to get that coffee and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:14.520
also because you didn't plan ahead.
You didn't wake up early enough.&nbsp;

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:19.280
Another excuse I sometimes hear at&nbsp;
church - at Bible study - is this:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:24.520
I could not spend time studying the&nbsp;
Bible this week because I was too busy.&nbsp;

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:27.480
Because I was too busy?
That's an excuse.&nbsp;

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:32.040
An excuse to try and rationalize&nbsp;
your sinful behavior.&nbsp;

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:39.520
You make time for that which is a priority to you.
So if you didn't make time for God that week, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:47.760
means you took other things and put it above God.
You made those things a priority while God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:52.600
says you have to make Him your priority.
Do you know most men who say that they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:58.840
Christians have never read the entire Bible?
They don't really make God their priority.&nbsp;

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:04.120
And you know, I've heard this saying a&nbsp;
lot, you know, in the Christian Community.&nbsp;

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:08.560
God doesn't call the equipped.
he equips the called, but what they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:15.920
don't understand is that is what the Bible does.
The Bible equips us so some of them sit back and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:20.920
they want God to do everything.
It is your responsibility to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:28.760
grow with Christ, to read scripture.
To take time, to spend time with God.

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:38.200
[2 Timothy 3:16-17]

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.080
Now listen to this.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:55.640
The Bible equips you for every good work but how&nbsp;
will you be equipped if you don't read the Bible?&nbsp;

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.920
You can't.
And as men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.320
you know we are normally&nbsp;
straight with one another.&nbsp;

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.640
So let me be straight with you.
Stop the excuses.&nbsp;

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:06.840
Spend time with God.
Read your Bible.&nbsp;

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:14.240
And then, stop to be just a hearer&nbsp;
of the Word and start to be a doer.&nbsp;

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:19.160
Because Jesus says if you love&nbsp;
me you will obey my commandments.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.800
[2 Timothy 2:15]

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:42.000
Nowhere does it say that only preachers or&nbsp;
pastors need to study the Word of God and know it.&nbsp;

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:47.800
It doesn't say that at all.
They cannot live your Christian life for you.&nbsp;

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:53.000
You have your own relationship with God.
When you die, you alone will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.680
stand in front of God.
Not your pastor, not your husband,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.680 --> 00:15:01.080
not your wife, not your children.
No one in your family.&nbsp;

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:03.480
None of your friends.
You alone.&nbsp;

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:10.600
You will have to give account.
So let us stop making the same kind of excuses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:16.600
like the rest of the sinful world.
We are called to be set apart.&nbsp;

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:20.040
We are ambassadors of Christ.
We are in the world but we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:27.600
are not part of the world.
Let's go on to the next one.&nbsp;

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:33.200
Stop saying vulgar words like&nbsp;
the rest of the sinful world.&nbsp;

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:40.040
You know, I'm shocked when I'm ... when I hear&nbsp;
someone who said that they're a Christian and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:47.040
I just hear them speak these vulgar words.
I feel the Holy Spirit in me, ah that pain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:51.680
and they continue the conversation&nbsp;
as if everything is fine.&nbsp;

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:58.640
And they even use God's name in&nbsp;
vain, having no respect for God.&nbsp;

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:03.440
God's name.
Would Jesus do that?&nbsp;

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:08.160
Would Jesus speak vulgar words?
And you know I'm telling you these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:12.760
things because I actually really care about you,&nbsp;
because a lot of people out there are sleeping.&nbsp;

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:18.000
They think that they're Christians but&nbsp;
they're living like the rest of mankind.&nbsp;

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.600
So they're lukewarm or&nbsp;
they're not Christian at all.&nbsp;

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:26.120
They think they are but they'll get&nbsp;
a big surprise at the day of judgment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:33.680
and I don't want that to happen to you.
I don't want you to be self-deceived.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.080
[Ephesians 4:29-30]

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.840
You see, true faith doesn't&nbsp;
mean that you just continue to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:56.960
live in sin and don't care about it at all.
Paul wrote about this in detail, in Romans.&nbsp;

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:59.600
The rest of the New Testament&nbsp;
talks about it as well.&nbsp;

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:03.840
Faith without works is dead.
In James, faith is not like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:10.320
jacket that you just sometimes put on&nbsp;
and take off when you feel like it.&nbsp;

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:15.040
You have been changed.
God Himself changed you.&nbsp;

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:19.840
He did a work of regeneration and gave you&nbsp;
the Holy Spirit, which means you have a whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:25.720
new spiritual nature within you.
And then if you do sin the Holy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:29.120
Spirit will convict you.
You'll feel bad about it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:32.200
until you can't take it anymore.
And you'll say God, please forgive me.&nbsp;

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:33.480
I'm sorry.
I don't want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:41.680
live the way I used to live anymore.
If that regeneration did not happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:46.240
if you didn't truly repent and accept Jesus&nbsp;
Christ as Lord and Savior, it's not a thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:49.200
that you grow up as in a tradition.
Oh, I'm just now Christian.&nbsp;

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:55.960
No, you need to be a reborn Christian.
John 3, Jesus talks about in detail.&nbsp;

00:17:55.960 --> 00:18:00.520
If you didn't truly accept Jesus Christ as&nbsp;
Lord and Savior, and He came to change you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:05.120
give you the Holy Spirit, then&nbsp;
you are not a Christian even if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:09.960
you grew up in a Christian home or go&nbsp;
to church or read your Bible sometimes.

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.840
[2 Corinthians 5:17]

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:31.080
People will be judged by every&nbsp;
careless word they speak.&nbsp;

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:36.520
So with your new lifestyle it is impossible to&nbsp;
say the same kind of things that you used to say.&nbsp;

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:42.440
Vulgar words - bad words - and even&nbsp;
breaking people down in the flesh.&nbsp;

00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:47.040
You are supposed to be the light of the world.

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.120
[Matthew 12:35-37]

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:18.320
If you truly are a Christian&nbsp;
man, why would you want to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:25.760
dirty jokes and speak vulgar words?
I ask you again, would Jesus do that?

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:27.640
[Ephesians 5:4]

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:49.280
How have you been living your life recently?&nbsp;

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:53.480
I'm just talking about vulgar words&nbsp;
but there might be other sin as well.&nbsp;

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:59.160
How have you been living your life recently?
Be brutally honest with yourself.&nbsp;

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:07.080
This is important because if you would&nbsp;
die today, how will God judge you?&nbsp;

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:13.120
The reason you're still alive means that&nbsp;
God is still giving you a time of grace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:19.600
and every time you take that breath&nbsp;
it is a breath closer to your death.&nbsp;

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:26.240
Then that time of grace is&nbsp;
done and then it is judgment.&nbsp;

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:30.400
And then you will stand in&nbsp;
front of God who is love, yes.&nbsp;

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:41.120
But He is also righteous, because He is holy.
Let's move on to the next one.

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.920
Stop being lazy.&nbsp;

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:49.400
Spiritual laziness is sin.
Paul tells us in Romans 12:11:

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:49.880
[Romans 12:11]

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.600
This is a lot more important than you think.&nbsp;

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:04.120
And I believe that we should preach&nbsp;
about this a lot more in church.&nbsp;

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:10.640
Let me read you something very interesting.
From my book, Bold Pursuit, a 90-day devotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:17.200
for men seeking the heart of God.
Day 48: Someone once said:

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:45.760
The Greek word translated as laziness in the&nbsp;
Bible is akedia, which means the absence of care.&nbsp;

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:50.160
This kind of laziness isn't caused&nbsp;
by a lack of physical energy.&nbsp;

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:58.360
It is a sinful condition of the heart that causes&nbsp;
people not to care about anyone or anything.&nbsp;

00:21:58.360 --> 00:22:01.800
The consequences of laziness are dramatic.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.400
[Proverbs 21:25]

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:14.920
Spiritual laziness is especially dangerous.&nbsp;

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:22.240
That's when we don't care enough to read our Bible&nbsp;
or go to church or pray to our heavenly Father.&nbsp;

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:26.680
The Bible has an interesting&nbsp;
command to those who are lazy.

00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.760
[Proverbs 6:6-8]

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:48.760
In its own way, the ant understands&nbsp;
that work is an investment.&nbsp;

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:53.760
It diligently gathers food while&nbsp;
its available and stores it away.&nbsp;

00:22:53.760 --> 00:23:00.240
The ant understands that a time of plenty is&nbsp;
the perfect time to prepare for a time of need.&nbsp;

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:06.960
So it puts in the work to prepare for winter&nbsp;
when provisions are scarce and life is harder.&nbsp;

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:10.560
That's the reality God wants us to understand.&nbsp;

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:15.880
Spiritual work is an investment.
Making the effort to study Scripture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:22.240
go to church and spend time daily in&nbsp;
prayer has immediate benefits of course.&nbsp;

00:23:22.240 --> 00:23:28.360
But it also has long-term benefits.
Being grounded in Scripture can help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:35.120
us resist Satan's temptations as it did for&nbsp;
Jesus during his temptation in the wilderness.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:37.760
[Matthew 4:1-11]

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:43.160
Surrounding ourselves with a network of&nbsp;
fellow believers can Inspire us to live out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:50.340
our faith in bold and impactful ways.
That's why Hebrews 10: 24-25 says:

00:23:50.340 --> 00:23:51.440
[Hebrews 10:24-25]

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:14.760
Staying in constant communication&nbsp;
with our heavenly Father can help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:20.720
us recognize His will for our life.
To enjoy these spiritual benefits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:20.720 --> 00:24:31.880
we must resist the pull of laziness and stay&nbsp;
disciplined in every area of our spiritual life.&nbsp;

00:24:31.880 --> 00:24:37.520
We must stay constantly aware that the&nbsp;
work we do now to understand scripture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:37.520 --> 00:24:39.600
build relationships with fellow believers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:39.600 --> 00:24:47.080
and maintain an open line of communication with&nbsp;
God will pay dividends for the rest of our life.&nbsp;

00:24:47.080 --> 00:24:54.040
Now, at the end of each daily devotional I&nbsp;
ask you to dig deep because we need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:54.040 --> 00:25:00.440
doers of the Word and not just hearers only.
So this is is time to examine yourself and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:00.440 --> 00:25:03.480
to be honest.
Dig deep.

00:25:15.520 --> 00:25:20.080
Ask yourself the following questions&nbsp;
and answer them truthfully.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:39.960
Take some time to answer these questions honestly&nbsp;
- truthfully - and if you want to take a look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:39.960 --> 00:25:44.600
my book, I'll add all the information for&nbsp;
you in the video description down below.&nbsp;

00:25:44.600 --> 00:25:49.120
Now, if you haven't subscribed yet, please do so.
We have a lot of videos on the channel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:49.120 --> 00:25:55.800
we bring out weekly videos so you might be&nbsp;
interested to watch one of these playlists here.&nbsp;

00:25:55.800 --> 00:26:01.160
And before you go, always remember.
Life is short, so please do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:06.760
waste yours.
Bye guys.

